  "body": "## What is needed\n\nUsers who cut simple shapes without a CAD model need a quick way to enter dimensions and make a normal operation.\n\n## Design\n\n- Add a `SketchRecipe` enum in `camcraft-geometry` for four shapes:\n  - Rectangle with width, height, and optional corner radius.\n  - Circle with diameter.\n  - Obround (stadium) with length and width.\n  - Regular polygon with side count and across-flats (or corner) diameter.\n- Compile each recipe into exact analytic `Line`, `Arc`, and `Circle` primitives in `SketchData` (`crates/geometry/src/sketch_data.rs`).\n- Refuse invalid dimensions (non-finite, zero, negative, corner radius larger than half the smaller side, side count below 3) by name. Never clamp silently.\n- Store `recipe: Option<SketchRecipe>` on `Sketch` (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`) and persist it in `SketchDto` (`crates/app/src/project/sketch_dto.rs`) with a `PROJECT_VERSION` bump.\n- Add `CreateSketchRecipe` and `EditSketchRecipe` undoable commands. Editing a recipe regenerates `SketchData` and marks dependent operations stale through existing stamp hashing.\n- Add a composite quick-op command using `BatchCommand` (`crates/app/src/commands/batch.rs`) that creates the recipe `Sketch` and attaches a normal `2D Contour` (`crates/app/src/operation/contour_sketch.rs`, shipped in `#1864`) in one undo step.\n- Ship MCP tools (`add_quick_op`, `edit_sketch_recipe`) in `crates/app/src/mcp/sketch_tools.rs` and add a compact form in the Stock/Sketch UI.\n\nClean-room rule: use plain machining terms only. Do not copy vendor UI labels, parameter names, or dialog flows.\n\n**Safety floor:** generates sketch geometry that drives toolpaths and posted G-code (`effort:high`).\n\n**Done means:** creating a rectangle, circle, obround, or polygon quick op generates, verifies, and posts G-code with no 3D model, edits in place, round-trips `.camproj`, undoes in one step, and passes MCP and UI tests.\n\nPart of #3045\n",
